      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A primary criticism is that the 15-minute city might lead to \"super-localism,\" potentially limiting the necessary social and economic interactions that require more extensive travel. Some argue the strong emphasis on hyper-localism can create social and economic segregation if not carefully managed with good regional planning. Furthermore, the high initial investment and required infrastructure overhaul can be a significant barrier for existing, established urban areas to adopt the model.",
